KNOWNBUG gcc16
main.cpp
--cpp11 --unwind 2 --depth 200 --no-unwinding-assertions --no-built-in-assertions
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
GCC 16's std::list uses __allocate_guarded_obj whose return type
__allocated_obj<_Alloc> is not recognized by CBMC's parser in the
deeply nested namespace context. The parser falls back to 'auto'
return type, the body is lost, and symex treats the function as
nondeterministic, causing path explosion. Root cause: parser type
name recognition failure for template class names in inline
namespace contexts.
